
🧮 DFDL Expressions (Dynamic Properties)

Topic	Description

Purpose	Jab DFDL property (length, occursCount, separator, encoding, etc.) runtime data se decide hoti hai, tab use hota hai DFDL Expression.
Syntax	Expression curly braces {} ke andar likha jata hai.
Language	XPath 2.0 subset use karta hai (e.g. ../count, sum(), string-length(), etc.)
Use Case	Dynamic (data-driven) parsing or serialization ke liye.



---

🔹 Example 1 — Occurs Count (Dynamic Array Size)

Message:

count=3;val=11;val=22;val=33

Property:

dfdl:occursCount="{ ../count }"

➡️ val element 3 times repeat hoga, kyunki count=3.


---

🔹 Example 2 — Dynamic Separator

Message:

sep=|;data=A|B|C

Property:

dfdl:separator="{ ../sep }"

➡️ Separator value message ke andar se li gayi (yaha |).


---

🔹 Example 3 — Input / Output Value Calc

Type	Description

inputValueCalc	Parsing ke time ek field ka value dusre se calculate karna.
outputValueCalc	Serialization ke time auto-generate karna (e.g. checksum, total, length).


Example:

dfdl:outputValueCalc="{ sum(../val) }"

➡️ Checksum field = sum of all val elements.


---

🧠 Summary

Static DFDL	DFDL Expressions

Fixed format	Dynamic format
Predefined values	Data-driven properties
Simple use	Powerful runtime parsing



