---

⚙️ DFDL Expressions — Property-wise Short Notes

Property	Purpose / Use	Example Expression	Explanation

assert::	Runtime condition check karta hai (validation).	{ ../countryCode = 'IN' }	Agar condition false hui → parsing fail.

binaryFloatRep::	Floating-point number ka representation choose karta hai (IEEE / IBM).	{ ../floatType }	Data me hi float type diya ho to uske base pe decide karega.

byteOrder	Endianness ::decide karta hai (Big / Little Endian).	{ ../order }	Agar data me "LE" hai → little endian parsing.

discriminator	::Choice me branch selection karta hai.	{ ../type = 1 }	Agar type=1 → int parse karo; type=2 → float.

encoding::	Text encoding runtime se set karta hai.	{ ../enc }	UTF-8 / ASCII jaise values data ke andar se lega.

escapeCharacter::	Separator ko escape karne ke liye runtime char.	{ ../escChar }	Example: \, ko normal comma treat karna.

escapeEscapeCharacter	::Escape char khud aaye to uske liye replacement char.	{ ../escEsc }	Example: \\ represent karta hai ek single \.

initiator	::Field ke start ka marker runtime pe decide hota hai.	{ ../prefix }	Example: int=5 ya num=5.
inputValueCalc	::Parsing ke dauran field ka value dusre element se calculate karna.	{ ../price * ../qty }	Derived value create karta hai during parse.

length	::Field length runtime me diya ho.	{ ../len }	Example: len=5 → 5 characters read karega.

occursCount	::Array ka size runtime data se decide karna.	{ ../count }	Example: count=3 → 3 elements parse honge.

outputNewLine	::Serialization ke time newline format runtime se set karna.	{ ../nl }	Example: LF / CRLF.

outputValueCalc	::Serialization ke time auto-generated field banana.	{ sum(../val) }	Example: checksum ya total field.

separator	Delimited ::data ka separator runtime data se lena.	{ ../sep }	Example: sep=

terminator	::Field ke end ka marker runtime se decide karna.	{ ../term }	Example: newline \n ya semicolon ;.

textBooleanTrueRep::	“True” value ka representation runtime decide karna.	{ ../trueVal }	Example: “YES” or “1”.

textBooleanFalseRep	::“False” value ka representation runtime decide karna.	{ ../falseVal }	Example: “NO” or “0”.

textStandardDecimal::Separator	Decimal separator runtime data se set karna.	{ ../decSep }	Example: , (3,14) or . (3.14).

textStandardExponentCharacter	::Exponent character runtime decide karna.	{ ../expChar }	Example: “E” (1.2E3) or “^” (1.2^3).

textStandardGroupingSeparator	::Number grouping separator runtime se lena.	{ ../grpSep }	Example: , (1,000) or . (1.000).



